proof_plan:
By [[De Morgan's Laws (Set Theory)|De Morgan's laws]]:
{{begin-eqn}}
{{eqn | l = S \setminus \bigcap_{i \mathop \in I} F_i
| r = \bigcup_{i \mathop \in I} U_i
}}
{{eqn | l = S \setminus \bigcup_{i \mathop \in I} F_i
| r = \bigcap_{i \mathop \in I} U_i
}}
{{end-eqn}}
Hence $\displaystyle \bigcap_{i \mathop \in I} F_i$ is closed, and $\displaystyle \bigcup_{i \mathop \in I} F_i$ is closed for finite $I$.
{{qed}}
